, Daskin MS. Strategic facility location: A review. European Journal of Operational Research. 1998;111:423–447. doi: 10.1016/S0377-2217(98)00186-6. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Church RL, ReVelle CS. Theoretical and computational links between the p-median location set-covering and the maximal covering location problem. Geographical Analysis. 1976;8:406–415. [ Google Scholar ] Daskin MS. Application of an Expected Covering Model to Emergency Medical Service System Design. Decision Sciences. 1982;13:416–439. doi: 10.1111/j.1540-5915.1982.tb00159.x. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Jia H, Ordonez F, Dessouky M. A modeling framework for facility location of medical service for large-scale emergencies. IIE Transactions. 2007;39:41–55. doi: 10.1080/07408170500539113. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Clausen J. Branch and Bound Algorithms--Principles and Examples. Department of Computer Science, University of Copenhagen; 1999. http://www.diku.dk/OLD/undervisning/2003e/datV-optimer/JensClausenNoter.pdf [ Google Scholar ] Brandeau ML, Chiu SS. An Overview of Representative Problems in Location Research. Management Science. 1989;6:645–674. doi: 10.1287/mnsc.35.6.645. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Current J, Daskin MS, Schilling D. In: Facility Location Theory: Applications and Methods. Drezner Z, Hamacher H, editor. Berlin: Springer-Verlag; 2002. Discrete Network Location Models; pp. 81–118. [ Google Scholar ] Garey MR, Johnson DS. Computers and Intractability: A Guide to the Theory of NP-Completeness. New York: Freeman; 1979. [ Google Scholar ] Densham P, Rushton G. Strategies for solving large location-allocation problems by heuristic methods. Environment and Planning A. 1992;24:289–304. doi: 10.1068/a240289. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Whitaker R. A fast algorithm for the greedy interchange for large-scale clustering and median location problems. INFOR. 1983;21:95–108. [ Google Scholar ] Mladenovic'' N, Labbé M, Hansen P. Solving the p-Center Problem with Tabu Search and Variable Neighborhood Search. Networks. 2003;42:48–64. doi: 10.1002/net.10081. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Resende MGC, Werneck R. A fast swap-based local search procedure for location problems. Annals of Operations Research. 2007;150:205–230. doi: 10.1007/s10479-006-0154-0. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Joseph AE, Phillips DR. Accessibility and Utilization--Geographical Perspectives on Health Care Delivery. New York: Harper & Row Publishers; 1984. [ Google Scholar ] Wang F, McLafferty S, Escamilla V, Luo L. Late-Stage Breast Cancer Diagnosis and Health Care Access in Illinois. Prof Geographer. 2008;60:54–69. doi: 10.1080/00330120701724087. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Luo W, Wang F. Measures of spatial accessibility to healthcare in a GIS environment: Synthesis and a case study in Chicago region. Environment and Planning B. 2003;30:865–884. doi: 10.1068/b29120. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Radke J, Mu L. Spatial Decomposition, Modeling and Mapping Service Regions to Predict Access to Social Programs. Geographic Information Sciences. 2000;6:105–112. [ Google Scholar ] Mitropoulos P, Mitropoulos I, Giannikos I, Sissouras A. A biobjective model for the locational planning of hospitals and health centers. Health Care and Management Science. 2006;9:171–179. doi: 10.1007/s10729-006-7664-9. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Canadian Cancer Statistics. http://www.cancer.ca/canada-wide/about%20cancer/cancer%20statistics/~/media/CCS/Canada%20wide/Files%20List/English%20files%20heading/pdf%20not%20in%20publications%20section/Stats%202009E%20Cdn%20Cancer.ashx Towards Optimized Practice. http://www.topalbertadoctors.org/ Alberta Breast Cancer Screening Program website. http://www.health.alberta.ca/health-info/breast-cancer-program.html Data quality index for census geographies. http://www12.statcan.ca.ezproxy.lib.ucalgary.ca/census-recensement/2006/ref/notes/DQ-QD_geo-eng.cfm Postal Code Conversion File (PCCF) Reference Guide. http://ww