earch, 2014; 14: 491. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Roy CM, Cain R. The involvement of people living with HIV/AIDS in community‐based organizations: contributions and constraints. AIDS Care, 2001; 13: 421–432. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Maxwell C, Aggleton P, Warwick I. Involving HIV‐positive people in policy and service development: recent experiences in England. AIDS Care, 2008; 20: 72–79. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Ponte PR, Conlin G, Conway JB et al Making patient‐centered care come alive: achieving full integration of the patient''s perspective. Journal of Nursing Administration, 2003; 33: 82–90. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Tsianakas V, Robert G, Maben J, Richardson A, Dale C, Wiseman T. Implementing patient‐centred cancer care: using experience‐based co‐design to improve patient experience in breast and lung cancer services. Supportive Care in Cancer, 2012; 20: 2639–2647. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Pope D, Tipler S, Kirwan J, Hewlett S. Implementing a patient‐led service for chronic conditions. Nursing Times, 2005; 101: 28–31. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 37. The British Society for Rheumatology . Best Practice Awards 2013 ‐ Case study: Bristol Royal Infirmary. Available at: http://www.rheumatology.org.uk/publications/best_practice/bristol_royal_infirmary.aspx , accessed 9 May 2016. 38. The Council of the European Commission . Innovative approaches for chronic diseases in public health and healthcare systems, 2010. Available at: http://www.consilium.europa.eu/uedocs/cms_Data/docs/pressdata/en/lsa/118282.pdf , accessed 6 January 2016. 39. Haywood H, Adams J. Patients'' experiences of rheumatoid arthritis education: a short report. Musculoskeletal Care, 2011; 9: 113–119. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 40. Abourazzak F, El Mansouri L, Huchet D et al Long‐term effects of therapeutic education for patients with rheumatoid arthritis. Joint Bone Sp